-- title:
--   LIDT definitions: LDT / MainInductionStep / Theorems / StageDataConstructors
-- statement:
--   This bundle contains constructors that convert answer-valued restricted slice data into the ordinary restriction, induction, and self-improvement records. The constructors preserve the stored failure probabilities and error bounds while forgetting auxiliary answer labels when appropriate.
--
--   Principal definitions:
--   - The restriction-data constructors build ordinary and answer-valued slice records from their probability conclusions.
--   - The per-slice induction constructors package recursive, main-induction, and hypothesis data.
--   - The self-improvement constructor transports the answer-valued data into the ordinary record.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
